[h1]OpenZone Games[/h1]
Table games for DayZ in the OpenZone series. Lay a deck out on a table, a counter or the floor: the mod works out where the others can sit or stand around it, and the game is played in a window while the characters sit at it. The first game is durak, podkidnoy and perevodnoy, for two to six players; others may watch. Made for the whole Ukrainian DayZ community.

[b]What you get[/b]
[list]
[*]Two decks: the classic one, and the stalkers' one with stalkers and mutants on its picture cards and two jokers. A card sharp's deck of either look has ten empty slots more.
[*]Every card is an item: a deck holds its cards in slots, and a game is dealt from the cards the deck really holds. Gathering the game gives the very deck back.
[*]Choosing a placement: a hologram of the mat follows your aim and says how many seats the spot has, standing, sitting or on the floor, or why it is refused.
[*]A card table in the look of the deck: your hand fanned with the playable cards lit, the others' fans of backs, the stock with the trump, the discards, the log. The cards fly, and the table is heard by everyone near it; every sound is the mod's own, made from numbers.
[*]Cheating: a card sharp's pen marks cards through the game's crafting, and any card can be studied closely. Whoever marked or studied a card reads it at the table; the others begin to notice marked cards, deal after deal. Three sleights a deal: slip a card in from your pockets, swap one, throw cards to the discards; the dealer works the deck. A sleight may show, and then the others may see it. The server's log keeps every sleight.
[*]Push-to-talk works while the window is open: talk while you play.
[*]A seat waits for a player who walks off; everything survives a restart.
[*]English and Ukrainian.
[/list]

[b]Needs[/b] Community Framework and OpenZone Core.

[b]For administrators[/b] One file, [i]profile/OpenZone/OZ_Games_Settings.json[/i], editable in the core's admin window: the poses, the radii and spacing, how long a place may stand idle, which games are on, and every cheating setting ([i]Cheating[/i] 0 switches marks and sleights off). The decks are in no loot table: docs/examples in the repository has the lines for types.xml.

[b]Licence, repacking, selling[/b]
You may repack this mod into your server's own pack, keeping the attribution and the same licence. You may not sell it, sublicense it or include it in any paid bundle. Running it on a server that accepts donations, sells cosmetics or priority queue slots is fine. CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 with the additional permission in NOTICE.

[b]S.T.A.L.K.E.R.[/b] The stalkers' deck and table use pictures from the S.T.A.L.K.E.R. games. They are created and fully owned by GSC Game World and are not covered by this mod's licence. OpenZone Games is a fan-made mod, not official, with no affiliation with GSC Game World. The original games: https://store.steampowered.com/franchise/stalker

Source: github.com/OpenZone-DayZ/openzone-games.

